==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|de|Kontor}} around 1720, from {{der|ru|gml|kontôr}}, {{m|gml|komtôr}}, {{m|gml|komptor||commercial branch; writing room; counting desk/table}}, from {{der|ru|dum|contoor}}, {{m|dum|contoir}}, {{m|dum|comptoir}}, from {{der|ru|frm|contoir}}, {{m|frm|comptoir}}, from {{m|frm|conter}}, {{m|frm|compter||to count}} + {{m|frm|-oir||instrument sufffix}}, from {{der|ru|la|computo|computāre}} and {{m|la|-tōrium}}.

Sense 'KGB' originated from a pun playing on another rare meaning of the abbreviation, namely {{m|ru|контора глубокого бурения|lit=deep-boring field office}}, in the 1960s.

